<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK VUB 9MO NET LOSS SKK 1.315 BLN.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK VUB 9MO NET LOSS SKK 1.315 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for the nine-month</p>
<p>period ending September 30, 1996: (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> After-tax result	    1.315 loss	    2.187 profit</p>
<p> Revenues		     14.850		  19.730</p>
<p> Costs			  16.165		  17.543</p>
<p>Reserves (including those for</p>
<p>  classified loans)	  9.691		   9.397</p>
<p> Interest received	   1.105		   1.312</p>
<p> Interest paid		 3.302		   4.569</p>
<p>Revenue from operations</p>
<p>  with clients		 8.224		  11.922</p>
<p>Costs from operations</p>
<p>  with clients		 3.553		   3.384</p>
<p>Revenues from hard</p>
<p>  currency operations	2.442		   2.589</p>
<p>Costs from hard</p>
<p>  currency operations	1.295		   1.736</p>
<p>General operating</p>
<p>  costs			  2.705		   2.304</p>
<p> Income tax		    1.239		   1.126</p>
<p> Basic capital		 4.078		   4.078</p>
<p> Total assets		174.583		 163.429</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Vseobecna Uverova Banka a.s.,</p>
<p>Slovakia's largest commercial bank. It accounts for about 60</p>
<p>percent of company loans in the country. Results are provided</p>
<p>by the Bratislava Stock Exchange (BSE).</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement, published by the BSE, that</p>
<p>its swing to loss was due mainly to accounting changes which</p>
<p>attempt &quot;to minimalise accounting interest on arrears which</p>
<p>could become irredeemable claims&quot;.</p>
<p>The statement also said that the bank had not accounted for</p>
<p>revenue from classified loans.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3688</p>
</text>
